  "explains": "Only api/openapi.json changes: the operation GET /invoices/{invoiceId} (getInvoice) gets a required query parameter expand. No code changes. The spec is read at both versions and the signature of every operation (method, path, parameters, request body, responses and every schema they reach through $ref) is compared: getInvoice differs in its parameters and is the only operation that does; the others, including DELETE of the same path, are the same. The changed operation is an area (the route GET /v1/invoices/{invoiceId}, reached at the first changed line of the operation) and an operation-changed finding, medium risk and high confidence, with the method key at both versions as evidence. Its client is the one of oa01: fetchInvoice, screen /invoices/:invoiceId.",
